.\" teachatty-server(1): the server. Plain man(7) macros, no build step: read it with man ./man/teachatty-server.1
.TH TEACHATTY\-SERVER 1 "2026-10-12" "teachatty 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
teachatty\-server \- the server for teachatty, a minimalist terminal chat
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teachatty\-server
.RB [ \-\-addr
.RI [ host ]: port ]
.RB [ \-\-tls\-cert
.I file
.B \-\-tls\-key
.IR file " | " \fB\-\-no\-tls\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-per\-ip
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-pipes ]
.br
.B teachatty\-server
.RB [ \-\-version " | " \-h " | " help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teachatty\-server
keeps chat rooms in memory and relays each message to the other members of its
room. People join with
.BR teachatty (1).
.PP
Joining a room that doesn't exist creates it, and a room disappears when its last
member leaves. The
.B local
room is the exception: it starts with the server and exists as long as it runs.
Anyone who connects without choosing a room lands there. Nothing is written to disk
except the server's own certificate: there is no history.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " \fR[\fIhost\fR]:\fIport"
Where to listen. No host means all interfaces; a host limits it to that interface.
Default:
.BR :7347 .
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-cert " file" ", \-\-tls\-key " file
Serve your own certificate and key (PEM) instead of the self\-signed one, e.g.
Let's Encrypt's
.I fullchain.pem
and
.IR privkey.pem .
Use
.IR fullchain.pem ,
not
.IR cert.pem :
without the intermediate certificate, clients can't verify the chain. The files are
reloaded when they change, so renewals need no restart.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tls
Serve plain ws:// without encryption. For testing only.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-per\-ip " n"
Maximum simultaneous connections from one IP address;
.B 0
means no limit, e.g. for a company behind one NAT address. Default:
.BR 10 .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-pipes
Refuse clients in pipe mode (\fIcommand\fR | teachatty), for rooms that want chat
and no build logs.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Print the help and exit.
.SH LIMITS
Messages larger than 1 MB are refused, and only the connection that sent them is
closed. Each connection may send 5 messages a second (bursts of 20) and 256 KB a
second; above that, the server reads it more slowly, so senders are slowed down
instead of anything being dropped. A member that stops reading (a laptop asleep, a
dropped network) is dropped after 5 seconds, so it can't freeze the room.
Connections from web browsers are refused.
.SH SECURITY
Traffic is encrypted with TLS by default. Without
.BR \-\-tls\-cert ,
the server creates a self\-signed certificate on first start and prints its
fingerprint on every start. Clients trust it the first time they connect and refuse a
different one afterwards, like
.BR ssh (1),
so share the fingerprint for people to check. With a certificate from an authority
the clients trust, they verify it like a browser does, with no pinning.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/teachatty/ " (usually " ~/.config/teachatty/ )
The self\-signed certificate and key, created on first start. Under the packaged
systemd service, this is
.IR /var/lib/teachatty/teachatty/ .
.TP
.I /etc/default/teachatty\-server
Flags for the packaged systemd service, in
.BR TEACHATTY_SERVER_ARGS .
Restart the service after changing it.
.TP
.I /usr/share/teachatty\-server/teachatty\-deploy\-hook.sh
A
.BR certbot (1)
deploy hook that copies a renewed certificate to
.I /var/lib/teachatty/tls/
for the
.B teachatty
user. Only used if you set up Let's Encrypt yourself.
.SH EXAMPLES
Listen on port 7347 on all interfaces, with a self\-signed certificate:
.PP
.RS
teachatty\-server
.RE
.PP
Listen only on the internal network:
.PP
.RS
teachatty\-server \-\-addr 10.0.0.5:7347
.RE
.PP
Serve a Let's Encrypt certificate:
.PP
.RS
.nf
teachatty\-server \-\-tls\-cert /etc/letsencrypt/live/chat.example.com/fullchain.pem \e
                 \-\-tls\-key  /etc/letsencrypt/live/chat.example.com/privkey.pem
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run the packaged service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudoedit /etc/default/teachatty\-server
sudo systemctl enable \-\-now teachatty\-server
journalctl \-u teachatty\-server \-f
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR teachatty (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR certbot (1)
.PP
https://teachatty.com/docs.html
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/daniel\-cmdline/teachatty/issues.
Report security issues privately, as described in CONTRIBUTING.md.
